{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":461832,"name":"Stanislav Chistyakov","username":"Stanislav_Chistyakov","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f14d63/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-08-09T09:48:54.896Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI would really like to have daily/weekly usage limits and better visibility into what is driving consumption, with the ability to set warnings, so it’s harder to accidentally burn through the monthly allowance too quickly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m currently on the Ultra plan, and something went wrong while I was trying to set up an SDLC workflow in one project. I \u003cstrong\u003eburned through my entire Ultra allowance in just 4 days\u003c/strong\u003e. Now I have almost the entire month left without normal Cursor usage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith a $20 plan, this is annoying but at least you can upgrade. With Ultra, there is no higher predictable subscription tier — the only option is to switch to usage-based billing. For me, that’s not really an option. I want a fixed subscription budget, not an open-ended bill. I can’t just stop development for a month, so I have to move some projects to another vendor just to be able to work till the end of a month.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt would be great if subscriptions had configurable daily and weekly limits. Something like “you’ve used the budget allowance for today, please confirm that you agree with it.” That alone would’ve been enough for me to stop and look into it before it was too late.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnother thing that would be really useful is a simple usage/optimization report to help understand \u003cem\u003ewhy\u003c/em\u003e usage suddenly became huge, or recommendations/warnings about potential problems. I’m currently using another AI agent to investigate what happened, and it already found several problems in my project:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI had MCPs for another project, but they were also enabled for all new projects by default. would be nice if i need to enable MCP by project manually, not everything by default on. If some MCPs are never used but still enabled would be great to see a warning or recommendation to disable them.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOne process was analyzing daily logs. Initially the logs were small, but later they grew x100 times while the cursor command processing them stayed the same. A report showing tool/command usage over time would have made this much easier to spot — maybe with warnings in case of significant changes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI’ve imported several libraries to develop AI agents, and they had examples of \u003ccode\u003eAGENTS.md\u003c/code\u003e for those agents (not for the IDE). Cursor imported all of them and they all became Cursor rules. may be a to have some report or even recommended prompt to check if all rules, skills are configured properly with some strange rules\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think daily/weekly usage limits, warnings, some kind of “what caused this spike?” report, build in recommendations/checks for project consistency could prevent a lot of these situations.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-08-09T09:49:03.151Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":25,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":128.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Stanislav Chistyakov","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/monthly-vs-weekly-usage-restrictions/162582/12","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Monthly VS Weekly Usage Restrictions","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/monthly-vs-weekly-usage-restrictions/162582/14","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Monthly VS Weekly Usage Restrictions","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/monthly-vs-weekly-usage-restrictions/162582/10","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Monthly VS Weekly Usage Restrictions","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-gives-no-warning-before-weekly-usage-spills-into-paid-on-demand/169679/6","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Grok Bot gives no warning before weekly usage spills into paid On-Demand","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":132014,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":true},{"id":462781,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-10T21:07:45.577Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/stanislav_chistyakov\"\u003e@Stanislav_Chistyakov\u003c/a\u003e Sorry to hear this. We don’t have immediate plans to add additional limits like weekly guardrails (in fact, the flexibility of the Cursor plan is one of the important product diffentiators and features that people enjoy, .e.g if you want to have a crazy weekend and use most of your plan in one weekend during a hackathon- you can!)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe best ways to keep usage tracked are as follows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUsage summary under the prompt.\u003c/strong\u003e In Cursor Settings, search for \u003ccode\u003eUsage Summary\u003c/code\u003e (under Agents) and set it to \u003cstrong\u003eAlways\u003c/strong\u003e. The default, Auto, only appears when you are already close to the limit. In the Agents Window, that readout sits in the status area right below the prompt. The same setting also controls the bar at the bottom of the chat pane in the classic IDE. If you see the Local / context row there instead of plan usage, turn off \u003ccode\u003eView \u0026gt; Status Bar\u003c/code\u003e so the usage summary can show.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDashboard.\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/dashboard/spending\"\u003ecursor.com/dashboard/spending\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/dashboard/usage\"\u003ecursor.com/dashboard/usage\u003c/a\u003e show remaining allowance in both pools (Cursor Models and Other Models), plus a per-day / per-model breakdown that can help explain a sudden jump.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs you know, Ultra has two separate monthly pools. If any Cursor Models usage is still left, Composer 2.5 and Grok 4.5 can keep you building without turning on on-demand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, while account sharing is prohibited, there is no policy that prevents you from having two ultra accounts, so if you’d like to sign up for another, that may be a potential avenue for you.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-08-10T21:07:45.577Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":73,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":383.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/dashboard/spending","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":7},{"url":"https://cursor.com/dashboard/usage","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":2}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":105146,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":462904,"name":"Stanislav Chistyakov","username":"Stanislav_Chistyakov","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f14d63/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-08-11T05:57:25.911Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for the reply.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA second Ultra account is definitely not an option for me \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/fluentui/slight_smile.png?v=15\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e It’s not convenient to manage two accounts. Please help me to understand if I can cancel my current subscription and go back to a free account while keeping the option to subscribe again later. It looks like I would need to terminate the account and start it from scratch to achieve it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI understand the point about flexibility, from my point of view, a warning would not remove it. In any case you manage your roadmap the way you need, so it is just a feedback. In my case, I normally spend around $20–40/month on AI coding tools for my personal activities. I moved to Ultra because of my wrong expectations that $200 is more than enough for every hobby project, based on experience from my work related activities with other vendors. So it is definitely my fault, I’ll check you recommendations. I’ve also seen that many users are asking for more detailed usage reports, so may we’ll see something like this later. I don’t have any question about the correctness of your report - just more details to understand misconfigurations and the way to fix in within the project, to have normal spending\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKind regards\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStanislav\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-08-11T05:57:25.911Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":13,"readers_count":12,"score":12.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Stanislav Chistyakov","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":132014,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":464232,"name":"Stanislav Chistyakov","username":"Stanislav_Chistyakov","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f14d63/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-08-12T20:13:12.052Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eOh \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/fluentui/frowning.png?v=15\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e i am not able to delete the account, just because i have some on demand spending and it require to wait till the Sep, 1 to complete the final billing.  Totally don’t understand why it can’t complete the billing it the time when i would like to delete my account \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/fluentui/frowning.png?v=15\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-08-12T20:13:12.052Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":12,"readers_count":11,"score":7.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Stanislav Chistyakov","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":132014,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":464283,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-12T21:55:57.414Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/stanislav_chistyakov\"\u003e@Stanislav_Chistyakov\u003c/a\u003e Feel free to send us a note at \u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e and one of our billing specialists can help you out! We’ll do our best to help you there on an individualized basis.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-08-12T21:55:57.414Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":8,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":27.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":132014,"username":"Stanislav_Chistyakov","name":"Stanislav Chistyakov","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f14d63/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":105146,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/9","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":488556,"name":"Steven Callister","username":"Steven_Callister","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/steven_callister/{size}/120538_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T05:34:39.761Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI appreciate the clarity on two accounts being okay… but it does feel odd mechanically that in some scenarios you’re better off having two accounts rather than using on-demand pricing \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/fluentui/thinking.png?v=15\" title=\":thinking:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":thinking:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":11,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T05:34:39.761Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":11.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Steven Callister","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137264,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/11","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":497016,"name":"Aniruddha Nath","username":"aniruddha.nath","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/76d3ee/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-21T13:56:43.100Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/kevinn\"\u003e@kevinn\u003c/a\u003e -\u003cbr\u003e\nI checked the topic you linked in your previous comment. However, the pay-as-you-go model could become quite expensive for us.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you submit a feature request to make the current \u003cstrong\u003eMonthly Guardrail\u003c/strong\u003e more flexible by introducing \u003cstrong\u003ehourly and weekly reset limits\u003c/strong\u003e?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, Claude currently provides a usage limit that resets every 5 hours, along with a separate weekly limit. A similar approach would work really well here and provide much more predictable usage and cost management.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt would also be great if these limits could apply to \u003cstrong\u003ethird-party model pools\u003c/strong\u003e, not just models such as Composer and Grok. For example, when we explicitly select a third-party model for coding instead of using Auto, it could have its own hourly/weekly allowance or a shared third-party model pool.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI believe this would make the offering much more attractive for developers who frequently use third-party models, while still letting you maintain reasonable usage controls. It could also help strengthen the product’s competitiveness and reach in the developer market.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":12,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-09-21T13:56:43.100Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":16.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Aniruddha Nath","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138970,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/12","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":505158,"name":"blockmodule","username":"blockmodule","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/a5b964/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-10-01T22:20:10.892Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eDean Rie asked me to comment on this thread, so here goes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince discussions about Cursor’s current monthly, hourly, and weekly limits vary greatly depending on each user’s usage patterns, if we were to listen to only one side of the argument and implement that proposal, there would inevitably be some users who are satisfied and others whose productivity suffers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is just a somewhat unconventional idea or suggestion of mine…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen signing up for or renewing a Cursor Pro, Pro+, or Ultra subscription,\u003cbr\u003e\nhow about allowing users to choose whether they want to use Cursor models and other models within a monthly limit, or select a limit pattern based on hours, weeks, or months?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat way, users could choose between a monthly, hourly, or weekly limit, allowing them to customize the service to fit their individual usage patterns, don’t you think?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI believe allowing users to choose between hourly or weekly limits and the current monthly limit would create a win-win situation for everyone.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you think?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"13\" data-topic=\"162582\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/a5b964/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-title__text-content\"\u003e\n      \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/monthly-vs-weekly-usage-restrictions/162582/13\"\u003eMonthly VS Weekly Usage Restrictions\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/ideas/feature-requests/5\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"5\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #9EB83B; --category-badge-text-color: #000000; --parent-category-badge-color: #ED207B;\" data-parent-category-id=\"22\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --style-square --has-parent\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003eFeature Requests\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    Dean Rie, thank you for your reply. \nWhen I listen to feedback from Cursor users, I realize that opinions are indeed divided into several groups, and I don’t think there’s a single optimal solution. \nIf we were to listen to one side and implement their suggestions, users would likely be split between those who are satisfied and those whose work efficiency decreases. \nThis might be a bit of an unusual idea, but… \nWhen signing up for or renewing a Cursor Pro, Pro+, or Ultra subscription, \nhow abou…\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNote:\u003cbr\u003e\nThis is an automatic translation from Japanese to English.\u003cbr\u003e\nSome parts may sound slightly unnatural.\u003cbr\u003e\nAlso, there may be instances where what I’m trying to convey hasn’t been accurately translated into English.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":13,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-10-01T22:20:10.892Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"blockmodule","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/monthly-vs-weekly-usage-restrictions/162582/13","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Monthly VS Weekly Usage Restrictions","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":130897,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/13","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":505169,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-01T22:28:28.037Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"aniruddha.nath\" data-display-name=\"Aniruddha Nath\" data-post=\"12\" data-topic=\"167802\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/76d3ee/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Aniruddha Nath:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you submit a feature request to make the current \u003cstrong\u003eMonthly Guardrail\u003c/strong\u003e more flexible by introducing \u003cstrong\u003ehourly and weekly reset limits\u003c/strong\u003e?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/aniruddha.nath\"\u003e@aniruddha.nath\u003c/a\u003e Thank you for the feature request. At this time we don’t have plans to introduce these types of limits! Grok bot has a weekly usage limit but it is separate from your regular Cursor usage.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":14,"post_type":1,"posts_count":9,"updated_at":"2026-10-01T22:28:28.037Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":167802,"topic_slug":"usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":105146,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/usage-guardrails-to-stop-burning-through-the-monthly-limit-in-just-a-few-days/167802/14","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":f